 "note": "Light switches flush on their finished walls and BW-013's signal outlet removed. The census ran before the passes at 9535800b and after each: pass 1 fbea083e, pass 2 32784e13, pass 3 f70c3c95 (receipts census_<tag>, with each pass's suites as census_<tag>_<suite>). census/ holds the packet census's per-plate lines before the passes and after each: rear face, gap to the physics and visual wall, the worst gap over a 13 x 3 grid of the plate's rear face against visible meshes and multimesh finishes (from census_after2 on), and small geometry nearby. 'Standing off their visible wall' after pass 2 counts the 13 hall plates seated on the 16 mm public wainscot backing, which is a multimesh finish in front of the blockout wall; the footprint column is 0 for all 144. At f70c3c95 LightSwitchModelTest 1449 checks, UpperLighting 9677, ConnectedWorld 57508 and HouseholdState 154, each 0 failures; ApartmentBatch 204 failures with labels identical to slice 85's; the domestic-objects fabrication module 10220 checks, 0 failures, with 1D's bell capture (images/1D_house_bell_native.jpg). replica_clearance.txt is the static replica's clearance table (sources/switch_replica), the source of the 4 mm figure; no runtime test measures clearance. Implementation verification captures and run receipts; not runtime proof.",
